\b\fs32 Launch guide: `international.ellesmere.com`\b0\fs22\par
\b Audience:\b0  Ellesmere College IT / DNS administrators  \par
\b Requested hostname:\b0  international.ellesmere.com  \par
\b Purpose:\b0  Point this subdomain at the \b Ellesmere College International (ECI)\b0  web platform on \b Vercel\b0   \par
\b ECI app today (temporary URL):\b0  https://eci-platform-seven.vercel.app  \par
\b Main site today:\b0  Finalsite (www.ellesmere.com \u8594? ellesmerecom.finalsite.com)  \par
\b DNS provider today:\b0  GoDaddy (ns43.domaincontrol.com / ns44.domaincontrol.com)\par
\b\fs26 1. What you are being asked to do\b0\fs22\par
Ellesmere College International runs on \b Vercel\b0  (Next.js). It is \b not\b0  a Finalsite Composer page, microsite, or Finalsite subdomain landing page.\par
\par
Your work is almost entirely \b DNS at GoDaddy\b0 . Do \b not\b0  move ellesmere.com nameservers to Vercel \u8212? that would break Finalsite and school email. Optional Finalsite work is limited to adding a normal hyperlink from the main site \u8212? not hosting the ECI app inside Finalsite.\par
\b\fs26 2. Critical: do **not** use the Finalsite subdomain pattern\b0\fs22\par
Finalsite\u8217?s standard docs say: create a CNAME for a subdomain \u8594? [keyword].finalsite.com, then open a Finalsite Support ticket so Composer can claim that hostname.\par
\b That pattern is wrong for this launch.\b0 \par
If international.ellesmere.com is pointed at Finalsite:\par
Finalsite will try to serve Composer content\par
Vercel will never receive traffic\par
SSL for the ECI app will fail\par
\b Correct pattern:\b0  DNS for international is a \b CNAME to Vercel\b0  (exact target from the Vercel Domains UI). Finalsite Support does \b not\b0  need a ticket to \u8220?claim\u8221? this hostname.\par
\b\fs26 3. Roles and hand-offs\b0\fs22\par
\par
Order of operations (important)\par
\b ECI team\b0  adds international.ellesmere.com in \b Vercel \u8594? Project \u8594? Settings \u8594? Domains\b0 .  \par
Vercel shows the \b exact DNS records\b0  to create (CNAME for traffic; sometimes a TXT for verification).  \par
ECI team sends those values to Ellesmere IT.  \par
\b Ellesmere IT\b0  creates the record(s) in GoDaddy.  \par
Vercel marks the domain \b Valid\b0  and issues HTTPS automatically.\par
What Ellesmere IT will receive from the ECI team\par
Copy the values \b exactly\b0  from Vercel\u8217?s Domains panel for this project. Do not reuse another project\u8217?s CNAME.\par
Typical traffic record for a subdomain:\par
\par
