\b\fs26 4. Pre-flight checks (Ellesmere IT)\b0\fs22\par
Complete these before changing DNS.\par
\b Confirm who can edit DNS\b0  for ellesmere.com in GoDaddy.\par
\b Search existing records\b0  for anything named international (A, AAAA, CNAME, TXT).  \par
   As of the pre-launch check, international.ellesmere.com did \b not\b0  resolve \u8212? treat this as \u8220?create new,\u8221? but re-check before you publish.\par
\b Do not change\b0  existing records for:\par
   - apex ellesmere.com\par
   - www (must stay on Finalsite)\par
   - MX / mail (ellesmere-com.mail.protection.outlook.com today)\par
   - existing TXT / verification records (except adding a new _vercel TXT if Vercel requests it)\par
\b Do not change nameservers\b0  from GoDaddy (ns43 / ns44.domaincontrol.com) to Vercel.\par
Confirm with the ECI team that international.ellesmere.com is already listed under the ECI Vercel project\u8217?s \b Domains\b0  page.\par
Agree a \b rollback\b0 : if something breaks, delete or disable only the new international CNAME (and any new _vercel TXT added for this launch) \u8212? never touch www.\par
\b\fs26 5. Step-by-step: create the DNS record (GoDaddy)\b0\fs22\par
These steps assume DNS remains on GoDaddy Domain Control.\par
5.1 Open DNS management\par
Sign in to GoDaddy.\par
Open \b Domain Portfolio\b0  \u8594? select \b `ellesmere.com`\b0 .\par
Open \b DNS\b0  / \b Manage DNS\b0 .\par
5.2 Add the Vercel CNAME\par
Create \b one\b0  new record for site traffic:\par
\par
Notes:\par
Enter only international in the Name field (GoDaddy appends .ellesmere.com).\par
If GoDaddy complains about a trailing dot, omit the trailing . \u8212? use e.g. cname.vercel-dns.com not cname.vercel-dns.com.\par
Do \b not\b0  create an A or AAAA record for international. Vercel serves this subdomain via \b CNAME\b0 , not via Finalsite IPs and not via Vercel\u8217?s apex A record (76.76.21.21 \u8212? that A target is only for apex domains, which we are \b not\b0  changing).\par
Do \b not\b0  point this CNAME at ellesmerecom.finalsite.com, eci-platform-seven.vercel.app, or any *.finalsite.com hostname. Point it only at the \b Vercel DNS CNAME target\b0  shown in Domains settings.\par
5.3 Add verification TXT only if Vercel asks\par
If the Vercel Domains UI shows a verification TXT:\par
\par
This does not move the domain to Vercel and does not affect Finalsite.\par
5.4 Save and wait for propagation\par
Save the record(s).\par
Expect propagation in roughly \b minutes to a few hours\b0  (rarely up to 24\u8211?48 hours).\par
Verify from your network:\par
dig +short international.ellesmere.com CNAME\par
dig +short international.ellesmere.com A\par
You should see a \b Vercel\b0  CNAME chain (hostname containing vercel-dns) and then Vercel edge IPs \u8212? \b not\b0  Finalsite\u8217?s ellesmerecom.finalsite.com.\par
Browser check:\par
https://international.ellesmere.com should load the ECI site (or briefly show Vercel provisioning while the certificate issues).\par
https://www.ellesmere.com must still be the unchanged Finalsite site.\par
The temporary URL https://eci-platform-seven.vercel.app can keep working; production traffic should use the custom domain.\par
\b\fs26 6. SSL / HTTPS\b0\fs22\par
Ellesmere IT does \b not\b0  need to install a certificate in Finalsite, GoDaddy, or on school servers.\par
\b Vercel\b0  issues and renews TLS for international.ellesmere.com automatically (Let\u8217?s Encrypt) once DNS is correct and the domain is attached to the project.\par
In Vercel \u8594? Domains, wait until the domain status is \b Valid\b0 .\par
If the browser shows a certificate name mismatch, DNS is wrong or the domain is not yet attached/verified in Vercel \u8212? fix DNS/Vercel config; do not buy a separate cert for Finalsite.\par
Force-HTTPS is handled by Vercel.\par
\b\fs26 7. Application-side tasks (ECI team \u8212? Vercel / Supabase)\b0\fs22\par
Ellesmere IT can treat this as the ECI checklist running in parallel.\par
In \b Vercel \u8594? ECI project \u8594? Settings \u8594? Domains\b0 , add international.ellesmere.com and copy the shown CNAME (and TXT if any) to IT.  \par
Confirm Production env vars on Vercel (NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, optional LLM keys).  \par
In \b Supabase Auth \u8594? URL configuration\b0 , allow:\par
   - Site URL: https://international.ellesmere.com\par
   - Redirect URLs including:  \par
     https://international.ellesmere.com/**  \par
     https://international.ellesmere.com/auth/callback  \par
   - Keep the existing *.vercel.app URL in redirect allow-lists if preview/staging still needs it.\par
Confirm portals (/login, /investor, /agent, /school, /team) on the custom domain.  \par
Smoke-test public routes: /, /schools, /investors, /agents.\par
\b\fs26 8. Optional Finalsite work (links only)\b0\fs22\par
If Marketing/International want visitors on the main school site to find ECI:\par
In Finalsite Composer, edit the relevant nav item or International page.\par
Add a normal external link to https://international.ellesmere.com.\par
Do \b not\b0  create a Finalsite Domain / Host Name for international.ellesmere.com.\par
Do \b not\b0  ask Finalsite Support to \u8220?point the subdomain at a Composer page.\u8221?\par
Suggested labels: \u8220?Ellesmere College International\u8221?, \u8220?International\u8221?, or \u8220?Our international schools\u8221?.\par
